Differentiating Equation  gives $\begin{aligned}
dX&=\cosh\omega\,d\rho+\rho\sinh\omega\,d\omega,\\
dT&=\sinh\omega\,d\rho+\rho\cosh\omega\,d\omega .\end{aligned}$ The cross terms cancel, leaving $ds^2=-\rho^2d\omega^2+d\rho^2.$

