Put such a black hole in a warmer environment. It absorbs energy, its mass increases, and Equation  says that it becomes colder. It then absorbs still more readily. Put it in a colder environment and the reverse runaway begins: it radiates, loses mass, becomes hotter, and radiates faster. Formally, $C_{\mathrm{BH}}
=\frac{dE}{dT_H}
=c^2\frac{dM}{dT_H}
<0.$

