p.src:
The class next tries a mountain-mass hole. It settles on the rough classroom value $M\sim10^{10}\,\mathrm{kg}$, hence $M\sim10^{18}m_P$, and obtains $t_{\mathrm{evap}}\sim10^{54}t_P
\sim10^{11}\ {\rm s}
\sim10^4\ {\rm yr}.$ This preserves the arithmetic actually carried through at the board. The verbal geometry used to motivate that mass—roughly $100\,\mathrm{km}^3$ of rock—would in fact be much heavier, and the exact lifetime coefficient would also change the result substantially.

